-- room for one more child: under two answering at once, go on; at two, wait for one to finish (wait4
-- blocking on any child). Each child is a copy of the machine (about 75 MB more per second of work), so
-- this bounds the server's memory however many readers arrive at once
s-room : Word → Proc W Word
s-room n = if wlt n #2 then ret {lzero} {W} n else bind (sys-call #61 #18446744073709551615 #0 #0 #0 #0 #0) (λ r → ret {lzero} {W} (if wlt r #9223372036854775808 then wsub n #1 else #0))
